"[{\"id\": \"D01\", \"item\": \"120-inch main route length LHWTP to Imlay City Booster Pump Station (IMC)\", \"quote\": \"extends approximately 26 miles from the Lake Huron Water Treatment Plant (LHWTP) to the Imlay City Booster Pump Station (IMC)\", \"source\": \"p.7\", \"unit\": \"miles\", \"value\": \"approximately 26\"}, {\"id\": \"D02\", \"item\": \"Main diameter\", \"quote\": \"120-inch diameter main\", \"source\": \"p.7\", \"unit\": \"inches\", \"value\": \"120\"}, {\"id\": \"D03\", \"item\": \"Normal operating pressure / design pressure\", \"quote\": \"has a normal operating pressure of up to 200 psi / operating pressure ... did not exceed its design pressure of 200 psi\", \"source\": \"p.7, p.17\", \"unit\": \"psi\", \"value\": \"200\"}, {\"id\": \"D04\", \"item\": \"Pipe type and construction\", \"quote\": \"constructed using prestressed concreted cylinder pipe (PCCP)... steel cylinder and concrete with reinforcing wire wrapped around the outside / was constructed in 1968 using embedded PCCP pipe\", \"source\": \"p.7, p.126\", \"unit\": \"type\", \"value\": \"embedded PCCP\"}, {\"id\": \"D05\", \"item\": \"Installation / service history\", \"quote\": \"installed in the early 1970s / has been in continuous service since the mid-1970s with the exception of one reported break in 1985\", \"source\": \"p.7, p.9\", \"unit\": \"date\", \"value\": \"early 1970s installed; in service mid-1970s; one prior break 1985\"}, {\"id\": \"D06\", \"item\": \"System share normally and at break\", \"quote\": \"Normally, 20 to 30 percent of the overall GLWA system drinking water flows are provided by the LHWTP / LHWTP was providing over 25 percent ... with an estimated flow rate of approximately 162 MGD\", \"source\": \"p.8, p.11\", \"unit\": \"percent / MGD\", \"value\": \"20-30 normal; >25 and ~162 at break\"}, {\"id\": \"D07\", \"item\": \"Break date-time detected\", \"quote\": \"On Saturday, August 13, 2022, at approximately 4:30 a.m., a sudden drop in pressure was noted / experienced a significant failure ... on August 13th, 2022, at 4:30 AM\", \"source\": \"p.10, p.126\", \"unit\": \"date-time\", \"value\": \"2022-08-13 ~04:30\"}, {\"id\": \"D08\", \"item\": \"Break location west of LHWTP\", \"quote\": \"flooding ... approximately one-half mile due west of the facility / failed approximately 1 mile west of the treatment plant / accessed ... approximately 1 mile from the treatment plant\", \"source\": \"p.11, p.126, p.128\", \"unit\": \"miles\", \"value\": \"0.5 (GLWA narrative) vs 1 (PICA) - see RFI-01\"}, {\"id\": \"D09\", \"item\": \"Failure appearance\", \"quote\": \"rupture occurred near the invert and on the south side of the pipe / Portion of the inner cylinder located approximately 100 feet from the break\", \"source\": \"p.128, p.11\", \"unit\": \"location\", \"value\": \"invert south side; inner cylinder piece ~100 ft away\"}, {\"id\": \"D10\", \"item\": \"Sole-conduit function and IMC reservoir\", \"quote\": \"main is the sole conduit to transmit finished water from the LHWTP west to the IMC / Potable water can be directed to the 20-million-gallon reservoir and repumped during peak demand or bypassed ... during low demand\", \"source\": \"p.9\", \"unit\": \"MG\", \"value\": \"20 reservoir at IMC; pumped or bypassed to 72-inch main west\"}, {\"id\": \"D11\", \"item\": \"Downstream mains\", \"quote\": \"From the IMC, flow can be pumped or bypassed to the 72-inch main that runs west / system was restored ... with flow from LHWTP to the IMC, and flow south through the 96-inch main to NSC\", \"source\": \"p.9, p.15\", \"unit\": \"inches\", \"value\": \"72 west of IMC; 96 south to North Service Center (NSC)\"}, {\"id\": \"D12\", \"item\": \"NSC historic mode\", \"quote\": \"Although the NSC was originally designed to pump water from the City of Detroit-based water treatment facilities (primarily the Northeast WTP) to Flint in the 1970s, this mode ... had not been used in more than 30 years\", \"source\": \"p.8\", \"unit\": \"years\", \"value\": \">30 years not used\"}, {\"id\": \"D13\", \"item\": \"Operating pressure observation pre-failure\", \"quote\": \"There were no high-pressure fluctuations recorded prior to the pipe failure / A review of operational data ... indicates that the operating pressure ... did not exceed its design pressure of 200 psi at any time immediately leading up to the event\", \"source\": \"p.16, p.17\", \"unit\": \"psi\", \"value\": \"no exceedance of 200; no high fluctuations recorded\"}, {\"id\": \"D14\", \"item\": \"Isolation timing\", \"quote\": \"GLWA team members were on site within two hours / Since the 120-inch was feeding the IMC reservoir during peak season, the break was isolated within five hours once the LHWTP was offline / 108-inch butterfly valve was closed at LHWTFP to allow service to Burtchville\", \"source\": \"p.16\", \"unit\": \"hours\", \"value\": \"on site <2; isolated <5; 108-inch valve closed\"}, {\"id\": \"D15\", \"item\": \"Repair pipe procurement\", \"quote\": \"120-inch repair/closure piece with a laying length of 16-feet was priority shipped from Texas ... arrived ... August 14 / An order for three additional pipe lengths was placed with Thompson Pipe Company ... South Beloit, Illinois / two new 16-foot-long lengths ... were made by Thompson ... arrived August 28 / total of three 16-foot lengths ... were replaced / Each joint was welded\", \"source\": \"p.13, p.15, p.18\", \"unit\": \"feet / lengths\", \"value\": \"16-ft laying length; 1 Texas + up to 3 Thompson ordered; 2 Thompson made; 3 total replaced; welded inside+out\"}, {\"id\": \"D16\", \"item\": \"Repair completion and return to service\", \"quote\": \"repair was completed on Friday, September 2 / main was returned to service on Friday, September 30 ... All restrictions ... lifted / City of Flint restored normal service on October 13, 2022 / duration ... August 13, 2022, at 4:30 AM through October 13, 2022\", \"source\": \"p.15, p.19\", \"unit\": \"date\", \"value\": \"repaired 2022-09-02; in service 2022-09-30; Flint normal 2022-10-13\"}, {\"id\": \"D17\", \"item\": \"Water volume to fill LHWTP-IMC main\", \"quote\": \"volume of water to fill the 120-inch main between LHWTP and IMC is approximately 81 million gallons\", \"source\": \"p.18\", \"unit\": \"MG\", \"value\": \"~81\"}, {\"id\": \"D18\", \"item\": \"BWA lifting sequence and impacted population\", \"quote\": \"By Sunday, August 14 at 11:30 a.m., BWAs were lifted for all but seven communities ... representing ... approximately 133,000 people / BWAs were lifted for the remaining seven communities by Saturday, August 20\", \"source\": \"p.13, p.14\", \"unit\": \"persons / date\", \"value\": \"~133,000 still under BWA Aug 14; all lifted by Aug 20\"}, {\"id\": \"D19\", \"item\": \"Emergency feeds during outage\", \"quote\": \"GCDC estimated that they were providing 2-5 MGD in addition to supplying City of Flint average demand 14 MGD / Cities of Lapeer and Imlay City, and Village of Almont each began use of independent emergency connection ... on August 13 / GLWA requested City of Flint close FL-01 valve on August 25 ... to provide water to Lapeer, Mayfield, Imlay City / DTE Greenwood ... could not be served while 120-inch was out of service\", \"source\": \"p.13, p.18\", \"unit\": \"MGD\", \"value\": \"GCDC 2-5 + Flint 14; FL-01 closed Aug 25; DTE Greenwood unserved\"}, {\"id\": \"D20\", \"item\": \"PICA inspection extent\", \"quote\": \"PICA inspected 0.5 miles east of the break and 1.0 miles west of the break / Total Inspected Length: 8,321.13 ft (1.58 miles) / Number of Analyzed Pipes: 525 / inspected approximately 1.58 miles ... on August 23-24 / accessed ... where three (~16ft) pipe segments were removed\", \"source\": \"p.14, p.126, p.15, p.127\", \"unit\": \"miles / ft / pipes\", \"value\": \"0.5 E +1.0 W; 8321.13 ft (1.58 mi); 525 pipes; 3 segments removed\"}, {\"id\": \"D21\", \"item\": \"PICA wire-break findings\", \"quote\": \"identified a combined total of seven (7) wire break regions / five (5) ... up to 5 WBs, while remaining two ... up to 10WB and 15WB each / No regions measuring above 15 WBs were found\", \"source\": \"p.126, p.134\", \"unit\": \"regions / breaks\", \"value\": \"7 total; 5x <=5; 1x 6-10; 1x 11-15; 0x >15\"}, {\"id\": \"D22\", \"item\": \"PICA anomalies and features\", \"quote\": \"Total Number of Anomalies Identified: 22 ... Suspected Manufacturing anomalies: 3 ... Anomalous Joints: 19 / Number of Pipeline Features: 13 ... Manholes (includes newly installed manhole at failure site): 9 ... 12-inch Blow-offs: 4\", \"source\": \"p.126\", \"unit\": \"count\", \"value\": \"22 anomalies (3 mfg +19 joints); 13 features (9 MH +4 blow-offs)\"}, {\"id\": \"D23\", \"item\": \"Pure East inspection extent/date\", \"quote\": \"On August 22, 2022, Pure ... conducted ... east of the failure location / inspected section spanned ... 0.62 miles / Pure ... inspected 0.62 miles to the east of the break\", \"source\": \"p.141-p.142, p.144, p.14\", \"unit\": \"miles\", \"value\": \"0.62 east on Aug 22\"}, {\"id\": \"D24\", \"item\": \"Pure West inspection extent/dates and gaps\", \"quote\": \"From August 23 to August 25, 2022, Pure ... west of the failure location / inspected section spanned ... 3.77 miles / sections ... from Station 14+84 to 23+47 and ... 65+31 to 68+19 were not inspected due to high water levels\", \"source\": \"p.168, p.172\", \"unit\": \"miles / station\", \"value\": \"3.77 west Aug 23-25; 2 gaps uninspected for water\"}, {\"id\": \"D25\", \"item\": \"Pure West EM results\", \"quote\": \"Pipes with no anomalies: 1,221 Pipes with broken wire wraps: 27 Total number of pipes: 1,248 pipes\", \"source\": \"p.169\", \"unit\": \"pipes\", \"value\": \"1221 clean; 27 with broken wraps; 1248 total\"}, {\"id\": \"D26\", \"item\": \"EM quantification limitation\", \"quote\": \"As the calibration process was not performed on any of the pipes from the 120-inch PCCP Main, the calibration curve was calculated using mathematical modeling ... / Variations ... will affect accuracy of quantification ... If calibration tests are done ... curve can be applied ... to refine calculated number\", \"source\": \"p.174, p.146\", \"unit\": \"note\", \"value\": \"uncalibrated - modelled curve; counts approximate\"}, {\"id\": \"D27\", \"item\": \"Industry PCCP failure benchmarks cited\", \"quote\": \"Over 100 million feet of PCCP is installed in the United States and GLWA system has approximately 2.3 million feet ... or 435 miles / GLWA has approximately 125,000 lengths ... overall failure rate ... about eight catastrophic failures for every 100,000 lengths ... PCCP manufactured from 1968 to 1971 were reported to fail just over once for every 10,000 lengths\", \"source\": \"p.16-p.17\", \"unit\": \"ft / miles / lengths\", \"value\": \"US >100M ft; GLWA 2.3M ft (435 mi); ~125k lengths; 8/100k overall; ~1/10k for 1968-71 vintage\"}, {\"id\": \"D28\", \"item\": \"HDR cause study scope (results withheld in available pages)\", \"quote\": \"GLWA tasked HDR to study the water main failure to determine the probable cause(s) under its LSIP. The study reviewed operational records, field investigations, and laboratory testing of the failed pipe\", \"source\": \"p.17\", \"unit\": \"note\", \"value\": \"HDR LSIP study - records + field + lab\"}, {\"id\": \"D29\", \"item\": \"LSIP inspection mobilization and tools\", \"quote\": \"Tools included electromagnetic survey to locate wire breaks, and visual/sounding inspections to determine if there was evidence of imminent failure / Xylem/Pure team inspected 4.4 miles ... August 22-25\", \"source\": \"p.15\", \"unit\": \"miles\", \"value\": \"EM + visual/sounding; 4.4 mi Pure total\"}]}, "